extends layout.pug

block content-header
  link(rel='stylesheet', type='text/css', href='/style/downloads.css')

block content-block
  .page-content
    h1 Downloads
    p Each GNIS-LD release is archived and available for download. Each release includes includes triples from the ETL process and the ones generated during inference. The current release is served live at the SPARQL endpoint and exportable from the #[a(href='/data') data] endpoint.

    h2 Release cadence
    p GNIS-LD tracks the USGS GNIS domestic names data on a #[strong quarterly] cadence. The USGS updates the GNIS dataset on a quarterly basis; the gnis-each quarter and processed with the #[a(href='https://github.com/DataONEorg/usgs-triplifier' target='_blank') triplifier pipeline], loaded into the live SPARQL endpoint, and archived here. Identifiers are kept the same between updates. Releases are also recorded in the dataset's #[a(href='/docs#metadata') VoID/DCAT metadata], so the archives can be machine-discoverable.
    p USGS occasionally removes features from their archives; these features can be found in the optional _historical_ archive download which is attached with each release. The historical features have the #[code usgs:HistoricalFeature] class attached to them along with the #[code gnis:lastAppearedIn] property which points to the release that last contained it. Despite being deprecated these features are still served by GNIS-LD for systems that require backwards compatibility.

    h2 Release archive
    if releases && releases.length
      table.release-table
        thead
          tr
            th Release
            th Published
            th Triples
            th Size
            th
        tbody
          each release, i in releases
            tr(class=i === 0 ? 'current' : undefined)
              td
                | #{release.id}
                if i === 0
                  span.current-chip Current
              td #{release.published}
              td #{release.triples}
              td #{release.size}
              td.dl-cell
                a.dl-btn(href=release.url target='_blank') Download
                if release.historical
                  a.dl-historical(href=release.historical.url target='_blank') + historical (#{release.historical.size})
    else
      p No archived releases yet — the current release is always available from the #[a(href='/data') live export].

    p.archive-note Archives are N-Triples, uncompressed. For loading instructions, see the #[a(href='/integrations') integrations guide]; for how releases link together, see #[a(href='/docs#lineage') querying across lineage].
